{% comment %}
  sections/featured-pills.liquid

  One subject, told four ways: a heading cluster, a strip of pill-shaped
  options under it, and one panel of blocks per option.

  ## Why it is not `sections/main-faq.liquid` with a different preset

  The FAQ's tab strip is a rail of names beside a column of answers — the
  question is which answer you want, and the strip is a table of contents. This
  is the opposite reading: four facets of the *same* product, each a small
  composition of its own, and the strip is a set of equally weighted choices
  rather than a list to walk down. That is why the options carry a mark rather
  than only a word, and why the panel is a full-width stage instead of a column
  of prose.

  A merchant who wants questions and answers should reach for the FAQ. A
  merchant who has one product and four stories about it — what is in it, how it
  works, where it comes from, what the company believes — should reach for this.

  ## What this file is, and what it is not

  It is the frame, the two axes and the background. Everything with content in
  it is a block, and every block that only makes sense here is private:

    Pill tabs        `blocks/_featured-pills-tabs.liquid`
    One pill + panel `blocks/_featured-pills-tab.liquid`
    Checklist row    `blocks/_featured-pills-check.liquid`
    Step card        `blocks/_featured-pills-step.liquid`

  Private — the leading underscore — because each one is a piece of this
  composition rather than a component the theme offers. A checklist row dropped
  into a footer is a row with nothing to be a row of; a panel outside a strip is
  a `role="tabpanel"` with no tab. They are addable here and nowhere else.

  Everything else the preset builds with is a block the theme already had: the
  heading cluster is a **Section header** holding a **Subheading** and a
  **Text**, and the panels are **Group**, **Card content**, **Image card**,
  **Image**, **Button** and **Highlight** — none of which knows it is in this
  section.

  ## The shell is `sections/featured-offer.liquid`'s, setting id for setting id

  Container, colour scheme, background media, the four border widths, the eight
  corner radii behind a Desktop/Mobile switch, the gaps behind another, the
  minimum height, the margins, the stack layer and the whole spacing group —
  every id here is one that section already carries, and both reach them through
  `snippets/spacing.liquid`, `snippets/background-media.liquid` and
  `snippets/container.liquid` rather than reimplementing any of it. A merchant
  who has arranged a Featured offer has arranged this one.

  What it adds is nothing. That is the point: a fifth section with a fifth
  vocabulary for padding is a fifth place to look for the same slider.

  ## The layout is a flex container of the section's own children

  The heading cluster sits above the strip because they are siblings in a
  column, not because a selector went looking for either of them. A merchant who
  deletes the heading is left with a section that still lays out, and one who
  switches **Direction** to Horizontal gets the heading beside the strip without
  a second preset existing to describe that arrangement.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings

  comment
    The background is the colour scheme's until the merchant says otherwise:
    either a colour of their own — the soft wash the preset ships — or a picture
    behind the whole section.

    The colour is emitted as a real `background` declaration rather than a
    custom property because `color-scheme-container` paints a background *and* a
    gradient image, and only the shorthand clears both.
  endcomment
  assign background_media = s.background_media | default: 'none'
  assign has_background_media = false
  if background_media != 'none'
    assign has_background_media = true
  endif

  assign background_paint = ''
  if has_background_media == false
    assign background_paint = s.background_color | default: ''
  endif

  comment
    ---- the frame ----

    One width per side rather than one for the box, summed into `border_any` so
    the three properties are emitted only when at least one side is drawn — a
    zero-width border with a colour on it is three declarations that paint
    nothing.

    Opacity goes into the colour rather than onto the element: `opacity` on the
    section would fade the panels along with their frame. With no colour picked
    the border is `currentColor`, which the colour filters cannot take an alpha
    channel from, so `color-mix` does the same fade in the browser instead and
    both paths honour the slider.

    Identical to `sections/featured-offer.liquid` and
    `sections/expert-quote.liquid` by construction, not by coincidence — same
    ids, same resolution, same stylesheet shape.
  endcomment
  assign border_line = s.border_style | default: 'none'

  assign bw_top = 0
  assign bw_right = 0
  assign bw_bottom = 0
  assign bw_left = 0
  assign border_any = 0

  if border_line != 'none'
    assign bw_top = s.border_width_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_right = s.border_width_right | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_bottom = s.border_width_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign bw_left = s.border_width_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
    assign border_any = bw_top | plus: bw_right | plus: bw_bottom | plus: bw_left

    assign border_percent = s.border_opacity | default: 100 | plus: 0
    if s.border_color == blank
      assign border_paint = 'color-mix(in srgb, currentColor ' | append: border_percent | append: '%, transparent)'
    else
      assign border_alpha = border_percent | divided_by: 100.0
      assign border_paint = s.border_color | color_modify: 'alpha', border_alpha
    endif
  endif

  comment
    ---- corners ----

    Four corners, twice — one set per device, behind the same Desktop/Mobile
    switch the padding and the gaps already use.

    They reach CSS as a single border-radius shorthand, in the order that
    property takes — top-left, top-right, bottom-right, bottom-left. Nothing in
    the stylesheet reads them as a bare number, which is what makes sending a
    shorthand safe.

    A phone gets its own four because the same number does not read the same at
    both widths: 40px is a soft lift across 1400px and a heavy scoop out of a
    390px screen. Each mobile corner falls back to its desktop value when the
    setting is missing entirely, so a section saved before these existed keeps
    one shape at every width.
  endcomment
  assign r_tl = s.border_radius_top_left | default: 40 | plus: 0
  assign r_tr = s.border_radius_top_right | default: 40 | plus: 0
  assign r_bl = s.border_radius_bottom_left | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign r_br = s.border_radius_bottom_right | default: 0 | plus: 0

  assign r_tl_m = s.border_radius_top_left_mobile | default: r_tl | plus: 0
  assign r_tr_m = s.border_radius_top_right_mobile | default: r_tr | plus: 0
  assign r_bl_m = s.border_radius_bottom_left_mobile | default: r_bl | plus: 0
  assign r_br_m = s.border_radius_bottom_right_mobile | default: r_br | plus: 0

  assign margin_top = s.margin_top | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign margin_bottom = s.margin_bottom | default: 0 | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- the floor ----

    A minimum, not a height. The section grows past it whenever a panel needs
    the room — and the four panels here are four different heights by nature, so
    the floor is what stops the page jumping as the customer moves between them.

    Zero is the off switch and is what an untouched section carries, which is
    why this is emitted unconditionally: `min-block-size: 0px` is what the box
    would do anyway, so there is no state where writing it changes a layout that
    was not asking for it.
  endcomment
  assign min_height = s.min_height | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign min_height_mobile = s.min_height_mobile | default: min_height | plus: 0

  comment
    ---- layout ----

    The Group block's vocabulary rather than a second one invented here:
    Alignment is always the horizontal axis and Position always the vertical,
    and `assets/base.css` decides which CSS property reads which from the
    direction. `snippets/group.liquid` sets out why that swap lives in one place.

    This file does not guess which child is which. Horizontal is a flex row of
    the section's own children, so the heading cluster and the strip sit side by
    side because they are siblings.
  endcomment
  assign direction = s.direction | default: 'column'
  assign is_row = false
  if direction == 'row'
    assign is_row = true
  endif

  comment
    Two settings, one control. The horizontal list carries the distribution
    options on top of the three alignments, because on a row they land on the
    same `justify-content` and only one of the two could win. On a column they
    would be inert, so that list is the plain three and the merchant never sees
    an option that does nothing.
  endcomment
  if is_row
    assign alignment_setting = s.alignment_row | default: 'center'
  else
    assign alignment_setting = s.alignment | default: 'center'
  endif

  case alignment_setting
    when 'center'
      assign alignment_axis = 'center'
    when 'end'
      assign alignment_axis = 'end'
    else
      assign alignment_axis = 'start'
  endcase

  comment
    The alignment with the distribution folded in, and the plain one beside it.
    They differ exactly when a distribution is chosen, and the phone stack needs
    the plain one: `space-between` is valid on the `justify-content` it feeds on
    a desktop row and invalid on the `align-items` it would feed once stacked.
  endcomment
  assign inline_axis = alignment_axis
  if is_row
    case alignment_setting
      when 'space-between', 'space-around', 'space-evenly'
        assign inline_axis = alignment_setting
    endcase
  endif

  case s.position
    when 'center'
      assign block_axis = 'center'
    when 'end'
      assign block_axis = 'end'
    when 'stretch'
      assign block_axis = 'stretch'
    else
      assign block_axis = 'start'
  endcase

  comment
    ---- the gaps ----

    A Desktop/Mobile pair behind one switch, the shape every other section in
    the theme uses. Both pairs are published unconditionally and
    `assets/base.css` picks which applies at a given width, because the pair the
    merchant is not looking at in the editor is still the pair the other
    breakpoint renders.

    `plus: 0` rather than `default` alone, which would replace a deliberate 0 —
    a gap a merchant can legitimately want when the strip is meant to sit flush
    under the heading. Each mobile axis falls back to its desktop value when the
    setting is absent entirely, so a section saved before the mobile pair existed
    renders as it did; one added since gets the schema default, which is half the
    desktop one.
  endcomment
  assign gap_x = s.gap_horizontal | default: 40 | plus: 0
  assign gap_y = s.gap_vertical | default: 40 | plus: 0
  assign gap_x_mobile = s.gap_horizontal_mobile | default: gap_x | plus: 0
  assign gap_y_mobile = s.gap_vertical_mobile | default: gap_y | plus: 0

  assign content_classes = 'featured-pills__content featured-pills__content--' | append: direction
  if is_row and s.stack_on_mobile
    assign content_classes = content_classes | append: ' featured-pills__content--stack-mobile'
  endif

  comment
    Reverse is `flex-direction: row-reverse`, not a second ordering of the
    blocks — the markup stays in the order a screen reader and a keyboard read
    it, and only the paint order changes. That is also why it is row-only: a
    reversed *column* would put the panels above the heading that names them for
    everybody using the page without sight of it.
  endcomment
  if is_row and s.reverse
    assign content_classes = content_classes | append: ' featured-pills__content--reverse'
  endif
-%}

{%- capture content_style -%}
  --featured-pills-gap-x: {{ gap_x }}px;
  --featured-pills-gap-y: {{ gap_y }}px;
  --featured-pills-gap-x-mobile: {{ gap_x_mobile }}px;
  --featured-pills-gap-y-mobile: {{ gap_y_mobile }}px;
  --featured-pills-inline: {{ inline_axis }};
  --featured-pills-align: {{ alignment_axis }};
  --featured-pills-block: {{ block_axis }};
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- capture section_style -%}
  {%- render 'spacing', section: s, declarations: true -%}
  --featured-pills-radius: {{ r_tl }}px {{ r_tr }}px {{ r_br }}px {{ r_bl }}px;
  --featured-pills-radius-mobile: {{ r_tl_m }}px {{ r_tr_m }}px {{ r_br_m }}px {{ r_bl_m }}px;
  --featured-pills-margin-block-start: {{ margin_top }}px;
  --featured-pills-margin-block-end: {{ margin_bottom }}px;
  --featured-pills-min-height: {{ min_height }}px;
  --featured-pills-min-height-mobile: {{ min_height_mobile }}px;
  {%- if border_any > 0 -%}
    --featured-pills-border-width: {{ bw_top }}px {{ bw_right }}px {{ bw_bottom }}px {{ bw_left }}px;
    --featured-pills-border-style: {{ border_line }};
    --featured-pills-border-color: {{ border_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if background_paint != '' -%}
    background: {{ background_paint }};
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<div
  class="featured-pills color-scheme-container color-{{ s.color_scheme | default: 'scheme-1' }}{% if has_background_media %} has-background-media{% endif %}"
  data-section-spacing
  {%- if s.stack_layer != blank and s.stack_layer != 'default' %} data-section-layer="{{ s.stack_layer }}"{% endif %}
  data-section-id="{{ section.id }}"
  style="{{ section_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
>
  {%- if has_background_media -%}
    {% render 'background-media', settings: s %}
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="featured-pills__inner {% render 'container', width: s.container_width %}">
    {%- comment -%}
      `children: true` staggers the direct children — the heading cluster, then
      the strip — so the section arrives as one cascade rather than as a wall
      that appears at once. The stagger is a setting; at its default of 0 they
      simply arrive together.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <motion-effect
      class="{{ content_classes }}"
      data-easing="outQuint"
      style="{{ content_style | strip_newlines | strip }}"
      {% render 'motion-attrs', kind: 'text', section: s, children: true %}
    >
      {% content_for 'blocks' %}
    </motion-effect>
  </div>
</div>

{%- comment -%}
  Every setting below is a control a merchant reaches in the editor, and the
  schema is one element's styling surface: splitting it to get under Theme
  Check's count of 40 would split the thing the settings style.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% # theme-check-disable ExcessiveSettingsCount %}
{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:sections.featured_pills.name",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "section",
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "_featured-pills-tabs" },
    { "type": "_featured-pills-group" },
    { "type": "@theme" },
    { "type": "@app" }
  ],
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:sections.featured_pills.paragraphs.blocks"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "container_width",
      "label": "t:shared.container.width.label",
      "info": "t:shared.container.width.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "edge", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "wide", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "standard", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "compact", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__4.label" },
        { "value": "custom", "label": "t:shared.container.width.options__5.label" }
      ],
      "default": "standard"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:blocks.group.headers.layout" },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "direction",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.direction.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "column", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.direction.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "row", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.direction.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "column"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "reverse",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.reverse.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.reverse.info",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "stack_on_mobile",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.stack_on_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:blocks.group.settings.stack_on_mobile.info",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "center",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'column' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "alignment_row",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.alignment.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "space-between", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.distribution.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "space-around", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.distribution.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "space-evenly", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.distribution.options__4.label" }
      ],
      "default": "center",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "position",
      "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "start", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "center", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "end", "label": "t:blocks.group.settings.position.options__3.label" },
        { "value": "stretch", "label": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.position.options__4.label" }
      ],
      "default": "start",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.direction == 'row' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "gap_device",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "desktop", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "mobile", "label": "t:shared.spacing.devices.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "desktop"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.horizontal.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 40,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.vertical.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 40,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'desktop' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_horizontal_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.horizontal.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "gap_vertical_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.gap.vertical.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 2,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 20,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.gap_device == 'mobile' }}"
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:sections.featured_offer.headers.height" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "t:sections.featured_offer.paragraphs.height" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "min_height",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.min_height.label",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1000,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "min_height_mobile",
      "label": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.min_height_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:sections.featured_offer.settings.min_height_mobile.info",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 1000,
      "step": 20,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "t:shared.appearance.header" },
    {
      "type": "color_scheme",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "t:shared.color_scheme.label",
      "default": "scheme-1"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "background_media",
      "label": "t:shared.background.media.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "none", "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "image", "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__2.label" },
        { "value": "video", "label": "t:shared.background.media.options__3.label" }
      ],
      "default": "none"
    },
    {
      "type": "color_background",
      "id": "background_color",
      "label": "t:shared.background.color.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.color.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'none' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image.label",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image_mobile",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_mobile.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "image_position",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_position.info",
      "options": [
        { "value": "cover", "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "fit", "label": "t:shared.background.image_position.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "cover",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "image_parallax",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_parallax.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_parallax.info",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "image_parallax_speed",
      "label": "t:shared.background.image_parallax_speed.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.image_parallax_speed.info",
      "min": 5,
      "max": 40,
      "step": 5,
      "unit": "%",
      "default": 15,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'image' and section.settings.image_parallax }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "video",
      "id": "video",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "video_url",
      "id": "video_url",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_url.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video_url.info",
      "accept": ["youtube", "vimeo"],
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "video_poster",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_poster.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.video_poster.info",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "video_position",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_position.label",
      "options": [
        { "value": "cover", "label": "t:shared.background.video_position.options__1.label" },
        { "value": "contain", "label": "t:shared.background.video_position.options__2.label" }
      ],
      "default": "cover",
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "video_loop",
      "label": "t:shared.background.video_loop.label",
      "default": true,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media == 'video' }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "checkbox",
      "id": "overlay_enabled",
      "label": "t:shared.background.overlay_enabled.label",
      "info": "t:shared.background.overlay_enabled.info",
      "default": false,
      "visible_if": "{{ section.settings.background_media != 'none' }}"
